==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|fro|desjoindre||disjoin}}, removed

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪsˈdʒɔɪnt/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔɪnt}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Not smooth or [[continuous]]; [[disjointed]].
# {{lb|en|set theory|not comparable}} Of two or more [[set]]s, having no members in common; having an [[intersection]] equal to the [[empty set]].

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|non-disjoint}}
* {{l|en|overlapping}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|disjunct}}
* {{l|en|conjoint}}

